Name: androidPermissionExists

Type: function

Syntax: androidPermissionExists(<permissionName>)

Summary:
Returns true if <permissionName> is a valid Android permission name

Introduced: 9.0.1

OS: android

Platforms: mobile

Example:

if not androidPermissionExists(pPermission) then
   answer pPermission && "is not a valid permission name"
end if


Parameters:
permissionName (string):
The name of the permission to check.

Returns(boolean):
True if <permissionName> is a valid Android permission name, false otherwise.

Description:
Use the <androidPermissionExists> function to check if <permissionName> is a valid Android permission name.

>*Note:* Permission names are case sensitive.

>*Note:* Android 10 and newer list most permissions in no permission group,
> among them "android.permission.INTERNET" and
> "android.permission.ACCESS_NETWORK_STATE". Older OpenXTalk versions looked
> for a name only in the groups, so <androidPermissionExists> returned false
> for such a permission there; it now returns true for every permission
> Android knows (needs the Java layer built from OXT-Beyond's source, which
> the runtimes asset carries from its next release).
